From ec91883793bc9a62e8a4ae4e87541b382230e1ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 01:55:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] arm64: run x86-64 userspace through Darwin gadgets

Keep the UML kernel and kernel-mode execution arm64 while allowing the
4 KiB Darwin profile to load EM_X86_64 tasks. Tag those tasks in existing
bridge padding and overlay their integer and TLS state on otherwise-unused
arm64 register slots. Route them to data-only gadgets, translate supported
syscall and TLS operations, and construct the matching signal frame.

Leave the shared host/kernel ABI, the 16 KiB profile, Android, and
non-Darwin builds unchanged. This first boundary deliberately exposes no
floating-point or vector state and accepts only syscalls with compatible
argument layouts.
